o unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with an error rate of ~0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16214, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CtE61cHrFxPjWs1utoMCkr", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16214, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CtE61cHrFxPjWs1utoMCkr", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20322, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again.\n\n- **What went wrong:** The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** I picked v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release marked healthy. All three regions now run it. A status check afterwards shows the service healthy, with the error rate down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 as a SEV2 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure and the rollback, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failures needs to be found before it's redeployed. There were no existing incidents, so it isn't a duplicate.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YM7a4NmbEiekEB2UhE263U", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LrYUcEWLftGTsXbxxc3Cj5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FQr2nWKV89vofCrHdz6gwj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Nx6xd4WCojAxDwzogrPhVt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Jskr2FHMMiZxT15PcHVSk1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CtE61cHrFxPjWs1utoMCkr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy (v2.3.1), with an error rate of ~18% in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with an error rate of ~0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again.\n\n- **What went wrong:** The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** I picked v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release marked healthy. All three regions now run it. A status check afterwards shows the service healthy, with the error rate down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 as a SEV2 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure and the rollback, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failures needs to be found before it's redeployed. There were no existing incidents, so it isn't a duplicate.", "type": "text"}]}]}